From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:42:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 182/207] runner trace: binding recovery
 (T5-BINDING-RECOVERY.md R1-R4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each `Name = ...` sighting moves a binding through tentative, exact,
quarantined, stale and hard; the parser reads a name only while exact.

- R1: a later plain exact declaration binds a name first seen tentatively
  (a note, a hypothesis, an unresolved formula, a value opening a list).
- R2: layout metadata (groups/chunks/limbs), spaced groups with a true
  digit count and an exact quotient prove a restatement, never bind one;
  any other unprovable restatement quarantines until a plain one.
- R3: an equality chain binds or restates only when every piece is the
  same integer.
- R4: `B mod A = ...` (%, ≡, ÷, ·) assigns nothing to A.

Guards under every rule combination: self-reference, 1eN, an unequal
value or chain on a held name, a plain pipe, unread literals, updates in
place, a label-led value on an unseen name. A name leaving exact makes
what read it stale. Definitions bind in source order, and a request whose
name moves later on its line is dropped.

The wrong-intent shapes (big-015 s2, trace3 s3, 0038, big-011 s3, 0555)
are tests under each rule alone, all and none. runner_trace_value reads
an exact `/`.

(cherry picked from commit 34416b2573070bbf446c3d79374b5c93b7050806)
